01:43:00.577 --> 01:43:03.873
Okay. If it's an order,
I'll take it. Thank you.

1274
01:43:04.673 --> 01:43:06.039
Good.

1275
01:43:08.851 --> 01:43:09.767
What do you think?

1276
01:43:09.792 --> 01:43:12.497
It's pretty impressive.

1277
01:43:13.875 --> 01:43:16.727
- Yeah.
- You're

1278
01:43:16.752 --> 01:43:18.155
You're good.

1279
01:43:22.201 --> 01:43:23.749
Three days, huh?

1280
01:43:25.462 --> 01:43:26.527
Yeah.

1281
01:43:28.138 --> 01:43:31.496
So, what are you gonna
do for the next 20 years?

1282
01:43:31.521 --> 01:43:32.555
You got a plan?

1283
01:44:24.894 --> 01:44:27.668
<i>Manual mode activated.</i>

1284
01:44:33.296 --> 01:44:34.397
Go.

1285
01:45:05.622 --> 01:45:06.634
That's not half bad!

1286
01:45:06.659 --> 01:45:08.261
Is full good.

1287
01:45:14.656 --> 01:45:16.447
Time go fishing, question?

1288
01:45:16.726 --> 01:45:18.313
It's now or never.

1289
01:45:29.886 --> 01:45:31.262
- Three thousand meters.
- Three thousand.

1290
01:45:31.287 --> 01:45:33.609
Probe signal good.

1291
01:45:49.946 --> 01:45:51.136
Now comes the fun part.

1292
01:45:51.161 --> 01:45:53.197
Grace go out on hull
to retrieve collector?

1293
01:45:53.222 --> 01:45:55.373
- No fun at all.
- It's a joke.

1294
01:45:55.398 --> 01:45:57.933
Oh, humor. Confusing.

1295
01:46:04.727 --> 01:46:06.077
You gotta be kidding me.

1296
01:46:06.102 --> 01:46:07.109
What problem, question?

1297
01:46:07.134 --> 01:46:09.171
It's fine. It's just

1298
01:46:09.196 --> 01:46:12.826
the sky is slightly on fire.

1299
01:46:15.345 --> 01:46:17.024
Words of encouragement.

1300
01:46:17.163 --> 01:46:19.432
You can't just say
"words of encouragement."

1301
01:46:20.403 --> 01:46:22.267
<i>Words of great encouragement.</i>

1302
01:46:22.292 --> 01:46:23.793
<i>Nope.</i>

1303
01:46:45.601 --> 01:46:48.113
- <i>Did you feel that?</i>
- Yes.

1304
01:46:48.138 --> 01:46:50.707
I'm not worried.
Are you worried?

1305
01:46:50.847 --> 01:46:51.802
Yes.

1306
01:46:51.827 --> 01:46:53.547
Great.

1307
01:47:06.944 --> 01:47:10.527
Collector is closed.
Move winch into position.

1308
01:47:13.575 --> 01:47:15.244
Whoa!

1309
01:47:21.724 --> 01:47:23.822
<i>How long is this
supposed to take?</i>

1310
01:47:24.834 --> 01:47:26.651
<i>Collector should be here soon.</i>

1311
01:47:26.676 --> 01:47:28.417
Yeah. It's here.

1312
01:47:28.442 --> 01:47:30.497
Amaze, amaze, amaze!

1313
01:47:34.644 --> 01:47:36.145
Careful. Collector important.

1314
01:47:36.579 --> 01:47:37.996
Yup.

1315
01:47:40.783 --> 01:47:42.648
<i>Altitude warning.</i>

1316
01:47:43.025 --> 01:47:44.979
Oh, hurry, hurry.

1317
01:48:00.196 --> 01:48:01.731
Hurry, hurry.

1318
01:48:12.342 --> 01:48:13.701
Grace?

1319
01:48:17.006 --> 01:48:18.806
Grace, status update.

1320
01:48:19.154 --> 01:48:20.730
Status update.

1321
01:48:21.324 --> 01:48:22.725
<i>Grace?</i>

1322
01:48:24.227 --> 01:48:26.084
<i>Grace is safe, question?</i>

1323
01:48:26.109 --> 01:48:27.682
I'm okay.

1324
01:48:28.390 --> 01:48:28.970
Good, good, good.

1325
01:48:28.995 --> 01:48:31.796
Come inside with
predator collector now.

1326
01:48:32.442 --> 01:48:33.942
Uh

1327
01:48:34.894 --> 01:48:37.263
<i>Why not moving, question?</i>

1328
01:48:38.868 --> 01:48:41.706
<i>Warning! Exterior
temperature elevated.</i>

1329
01:48:41.731 --> 01:48:43.900
Must move now. Go, go.

1330
01:48:52.189 --> 01:48:54.458
No, Grace. Bad
idea. Come inside.

1331
01:48:54.483 --> 01:48:56.184
I'll be there in a minute.

1332
01:48:56.209 --> 01:48:58.861
<i>No, no, no, no,
no. Grace will die.</i>

1333
01:48:58.935 --> 01:49:00.818
Can repeat mission.
Can try again later.

1334
01:49:00.843 --> 01:49:02.962
I don't think there
is gonna be a later.

1335
01:49:02.987 --> 01:49:04.368
Abort, abort, abort.

1336
01:49:04.393 --> 01:49:07.330
<i>Grace will die.
No-No-No-No-No-No-No-No-No.</i>

1337
01:49:38.207 --> 01:49:40.497
- Grace?
- I'm here!

1338
01:49:41.004 --> 01:49:42.423
Amaze, amaze, amaze!

1339
01:49:42.827 --> 01:49:44.112
Grace okay, question?

1340
01:49:44.137 --> 01:49:45.882
Well, I'm not dead, so yes.

1341
01:49:45.907 --> 01:49:47.341
Good, good, good, good.

1342
01:49:47.366 --> 01:49:50.008
Where is that noise coming from?

1343
01:49:50.033 --> 01:49:51.183
Noise is from all around.

1344
01:49:51.208 --> 01:49:53.910
It's loudest at port
side of bedroom.

1345
01:49:54.223 --> 01:49:57.846
The gravity's
tearing the ship apart.

1346
01:49:58.982 --> 01:50:00.585
We leave now, question?

1347
01:50:00.610 --> 01:50:03.178
We leave now, statement.

1348
01:50:13.970 --> 01:50:15.905
<i>Hull pressure warning.</i>

1349
01:50:15.930 --> 01:50:17.906
Hull bending in big
room below bedroom.

1350
01:50:17.931 --> 01:50:19.299
That's the fuel tanks.

1351
01:50:21.365 --> 01:50:23.476
- Oh. Bad, bad, bad.
- Well, it's not great.

1352
01:50:23.501 --> 01:50:24.693
- Bad, bad, bad.
<i>- Warning.</i>

1353
01:50:24.718 --> 01:50:27.321
Everybody, calm down. Calm down!

1354
01:50:30.974 --> 01:50:32.543
Try and keep yourself
together, Mary.

1355
01:50:32.568 --> 01:50:34.087
- Stop engine now?
- Not yet.

1356
01:50:34.112 --> 01:50:35.992
We need to get into
orbit or we'll crash!

1357
01:50:36.017 --> 01:50:38.786
I have an idea. First, no crash.

1358
01:50:38.934 --> 01:50:41.455
Then, not explode. Deal?

1359
01:50:41.480 --> 01:50:42.681
Deal!

1360
01:50:44.299 --> 01:50:45.647
Hold on.

1361
01:50:48.004 --> 01:50:49.453
Now?

1362
01:50:49.478 --> 01:50:50.880
Wait.

1363
01:50:53.510 --> 01:50:55.199
Now? Now?

1364
01:50:56.258 --> 01:50:58.094
Now!

1365
01:51:09.025 --> 01:51:10.460
Did we do it?

1366
01:51:32.048 --> 01:51:33.483
Why ship moving, question?

1367
01:51:33.508 --> 01:51:35.108
There's a hole in it!

1368
01:51:36.639 --> 01:51:37.613
<i>Hull breach.</i>

1369
01:51:37.638 --> 01:51:40.982
<i>Port side fuel
compartments 11 and 12.</i>

1370
01:51:43.953 --> 01:51:46.588
Grace. What happening, question?

1371
01:51:47.316 --> 01:51:49.986
The fuel is migrating to Adrian!

1372
01:51:54.870 --> 01:51:56.710
Eject bad fuel bay, question?

1373
01:51:56.735 --> 01:51:57.810
Yeah.

1374
01:51:58.788 --> 01:52:02.559
<i>Jettison port fuel tank
compartment 12. Confirm.</i>

1375
01:52:11.669 --> 01:52:13.212
Rocky!

1376
01:52:24.653 --> 01:52:29.090
<i>Jettison port fuel tank
compartment 11. Confirm.</i>

1377
01:52:29.264 --> 01:52:32.267
Eject other fuel bay.

1378
01:55:46.411 --> 01:55:50.249
One nanogram of Astrophage just
isn't enough to blow up a building.

1379
01:55:50.274 --> 01:55:53.365
The quartermaster gave him
one milligram by mistake.

1380
01:55:53.390 --> 01:55:55.484
That's a million
times the heat energy

1381
01:55:55.509 --> 01:55:56.695
that they're prepared for.

1382
01:55:56.720 --> 01:56:00.444
A measuring mistake killed
my entire science team?

1383
01:56:00.469 --> 01:56:02.960
It doesn't matter.
We have to launch.

1384
01:56:09.649 --> 01:56:12.281
If we miss the orbital window,
it'll set us back months.

1385
01:56:12.306 --> 01:56:15.340
Yeah, but if no one's trained to
do the mission, it won't matter.

1386
01:56:15.365 --> 01:56:18.090
Casualty projections go
up exponentially if we delay.

1387
01:56:18.115 --> 01:56:20.693
We launch on schedule with
a replacement science officer.

1388
01:56:20.718 --> 01:56:23.907
Okay, but

1389
01:56:23.932 --> 01:56:25.033
who?

1390
01:56:26.957 --> 01:56:29.711
I mean, that...

1391
01:56:45.439 --> 01:56:46.627
I'm not an astronaut.

1392
01:56:46.652 --> 01:56:48.047
I don't need an astronaut.

1393
01:56:48.072 --> 01:56:50.573
I need an expert on
Astrophage who's mission-ready.

1394
01:56:50.598 --> 01:56:51.934
I'm not ready.

1395
01:56:53.146 --> 01:56:55.914
I don't have any training.

1396
01:56:55.939 --> 01:56:57.207
You'll pick it up.

1397
01:56:57.262 --> 01:56:59.153
I'm not an astronaut!

1398
01:56:59.587 --> 01:57:01.394
I put the "not" in astronaut.

1399
01:57:01.419 --> 01:57:02.452
I've never done anything--

1400
01:57:02.477 --> 01:57:05.097
I've never done a space
wa-- I can't even moonwalk!

1401
01:57:05.122 --> 01:57:07.025
I haven't done the
whole pool thing.

1402
01:57:07.050 --> 01:57:09.043
No, no, no. This is just
we do for the picture,

1403
01:57:09.068 --> 01:57:10.170
for social media.

1404
01:57:10.195 --> 01:57:12.343
I'm not heroic in any way.

1405
01:57:12.368 --> 01:57:14.863
I get sick on an elevator.

1406
01:57:14.888 --> 01:57:17.201
Oh, perfect. There's
no elevator on the ship.

1407
01:57:17.226 --> 01:57:18.744
I cannot do this.

1408
01:57:18.769 --> 01:57:20.937
You're smart.
You'll figure it out.

1409
01:57:23.384 --> 01:57:26.327
This might be very hard
for you to understand,

1410
01:57:26.352 --> 01:57:28.077
but some people are failures.

1411
01:57:28.102 --> 01:57:30.129
Some people <i>don't</i>
rise to the challenge.

1412
01:57:30.154 --> 01:57:32.478
You've been present
for every major scientific

1413
01:57:32.503 --> 01:57:35.228
or strategic meeting
we've had on the mission.

1414
01:57:35.253 --> 01:57:37.265
You're missing out an
important part of the mission

1415
01:57:37.290 --> 01:57:39.245
which is the suicide part.

1416
01:57:39.270 --> 01:57:41.804
Grace, you'd be in
very cool company.

1417
01:57:41.829 --> 01:57:43.760
If you don't go, you die anyway.

1418
01:57:43.785 --> 01:57:46.930
Yeah, but I die
in 30 years with--

1419
01:57:46.955 --> 01:57:48.223
"With the rest of us."

1420
01:57:49.534 --> 01:57:52.936
You have no immediate family.
You don't even have a dog.

1421
01:57:55.487 --> 01:57:58.191
So, just so I'm clear

1422
01:57:58.216 --> 01:58:02.854
you're asking me right now to...

1423
01:58:02.879 --> 01:58:04.123
 give up my life.

1424
01:58:04.148 --> 01:58:06.084
I am. We all are.

1425
01:58:10.380 --> 01:58:13.024
- Can I think about this?
- You have three hours.

1426
01:58:58.202 --> 01:59:00.770
<i>Eye movement detected.</i>

1427
01:59:01.911 --> 01:59:04.013
<i>Good morning, Dr. Grace.</i>

1428
02:00:22.359 --> 02:00:24.627
I'll watch you sleep, pal.

1429
02:00:31.449 --> 02:00:34.672
But, uh

1430
02:00:34.699 --> 02:00:36.400
you gotta wake up.

1431
02:01:11.062 --> 02:01:13.064
<i>I'm not sure what to do.</i>

1432
02:01:17.572 --> 02:01:19.610
<i>Done everything I can think of.</i>

1433
02:01:24.929 --> 02:01:27.589
<i>I made him a heat lamp.</i>

1434
02:01:49.878 --> 02:01:52.410
<i>And he left me one last message.</i>

1435
02:03:34.262 --> 02:03:36.065
We have our predator.

1436
02:03:36.090 --> 02:03:38.672
Right now I'm
calling it "Taumoeba."

1437
02:03:38.951 --> 02:03:41.542
And I'm sure that
when you wake up,

1438
02:03:41.567 --> 02:03:45.166
you'll have a lot to say
about why that's a bad name

1439
02:03:45.191 --> 02:03:47.623
because it's just an
amoeba from Tau Ceti,

1440
02:03:47.648 --> 02:03:49.547
and we're putting "Tau"
in front of "amoeba."

1441
02:03:49.572 --> 02:03:53.145
But I would argue
there's an elegance to that.

1442
02:03:53.170 --> 02:03:54.104
A simplicity.

1443
02:03:54.129 --> 02:03:55.772
Let's not fight about it now.

1444
02:03:55.797 --> 02:03:58.627
Lets just-- We'll table it and we'll--

1445
02:03:58.652 --> 02:04:01.097
I did a test at different
atmospheric variables

1446
02:04:01.122 --> 02:04:05.175
and, fun fact, every
time I introduced nitrogen

1447
02:04:05.200 --> 02:04:06.218
it died.

1448
02:04:06.243 --> 02:04:07.439
And I know what you're thinking,

1449
02:04:07.464 --> 02:04:09.641
"Well, that's terrible
because that's a problem

1450
02:04:09.666 --> 02:04:12.758
'cause we need it to survive
in the conditions of Venus."

1451
02:04:12.783 --> 02:04:14.592
Obviously, I had to
figure out how to breed

1452
02:04:14.617 --> 02:04:17.520
a new strain of
nitrogen-resistant Taumoeba.

1453
02:04:18.482 --> 02:04:20.083
And guess what I used?

1454
02:04:20.108 --> 02:04:23.506
The breeder tanks that
we made with your xenonite.

1455
02:04:24.448 --> 02:04:26.050
And you know what?

1456
02:04:27.631 --> 02:04:30.062
Now we're just a
couple of very cool dudes

1457
02:04:30.087 --> 02:04:33.791
with their very own strain of
nitrogen-resistant Taumoeba.

1458
02:04:34.219 --> 02:04:38.146
Really, all we have to do now is
breed enough to survive the trip.

1459
02:04:38.171 --> 02:04:40.037
And you gotta wake up

1460
02:04:40.062 --> 02:04:44.048
because I don't know how to get
your half of the Taumoeba to Erid.

1461
02:04:45.280 --> 02:04:46.784
So

1462
02:04:46.809 --> 02:04:49.145
No pressure

1463
02:04:49.170 --> 02:04:51.906
but we did make a deal.

1464
02:06:11.796 --> 02:06:13.298
Shh.

1465
02:06:13.323 --> 02:06:14.925
Grace?

1466
02:06:20.317 --> 02:06:27.151
Rock, could you just give me a
little chance please to sleep a little?

1467
02:06:42.104 --> 02:06:44.606
Did we find predator?

1468
02:06:53.297 --> 02:06:55.833
No? Is yes.

1469
02:07:11.969 --> 02:07:14.142
Amaze, amaze, amaze.

1470
02:07:14.167 --> 02:07:16.928
Rocky breeder tank design.

1471
02:07:17.241 --> 02:07:18.174
Good job, Rock.

1472
02:07:18.199 --> 02:07:21.036
We can go home, statement.

1473
02:07:22.726 --> 02:07:24.461
We can go home.

1474
02:07:24.595 --> 02:07:26.465
Fist my bump.

1475
02:07:26.909 --> 02:07:28.505
Nope.

1476
02:07:28.846 --> 02:07:30.369
It's still not right.

1477
02:07:30.533 --> 02:07:33.203
- I'll do it.
- Good, good, good.

1478
02:07:33.810 --> 02:07:36.482
So what we do now, question?

1479
02:07:40.858 --> 02:07:42.091
We party.

1480
02:07:54.478 --> 02:07:55.713
Wow.

1481
02:07:56.299 --> 02:07:58.700
Is special clothing
for celebration.

1482
02:07:58.725 --> 02:08:02.895
You're making me think that
I have to, uh, up my game.

1483
02:08:03.100 --> 02:08:04.827
- What is this?
- If you don't mind.

1484
02:08:04.852 --> 02:08:06.899
- Rocky get one!
- There you go.

1485
02:08:07.290 --> 02:08:09.960
- Is good.
- Yeah.

1486
02:08:12.216 --> 02:08:14.751
It's not much. Just
a little something.

1487
02:08:15.211 --> 02:08:16.444
Your very own laptop.

1488
02:08:16.469 --> 02:08:18.003
My portable Earth
thinking-machine!

1489
02:08:18.028 --> 02:08:20.140
With all human knowledge.

1490
02:08:20.165 --> 02:08:22.999
- Thank, thank, thank.
- And just one more thing.

1491
02:08:23.024 --> 02:08:24.463
Yes?

1492
02:08:25.804 --> 02:08:27.284
What this?

1493
02:08:27.309 --> 02:08:28.777
It's Earth.

1494
02:08:30.475 --> 02:08:32.825
So you can remember me.

1495
02:08:41.558 --> 02:08:44.120
Rocky can't forget.

1496
02:08:47.392 --> 02:08:49.260
I didn't get you anything.

1497
02:08:50.934 --> 02:08:52.869
You gave me everything.

1498
02:08:54.539 --> 02:08:56.607
But if I were to
give you something?

1499
02:09:00.003 --> 02:09:02.105
It'd be pretty cool
to see your ship.

1500
02:10:20.618 --> 02:10:23.782
<i>I understand that you think</i> I'm
the right person for this mission.

1501
02:10:25.669 --> 02:10:26.878
But

1502
02:10:31.363 --> 02:10:32.997
I can't do it.

1503
02:10:40.444 --> 02:10:41.979
I can't do it.

1504
02:10:47.731 --> 02:10:49.767
You'll find a solution.

1505
02:10:50.180 --> 02:10:52.348
You are my solution.

1506
02:10:57.101 --> 02:10:59.141
My place is in the classroom.

1507
02:10:59.166 --> 02:11:00.972
Stop pretending this
is about your students.

1508
02:11:00.997 --> 02:11:02.466
It's so insulting.

1509
02:11:03.747 --> 02:11:06.230
Grace, we will lose...

1510
02:11:06.255 --> 02:11:09.422
a quarter of the
world's population

1511
02:11:09.447 --> 02:11:11.048
in the next 30 years.

1512
02:11:12.242 --> 02:11:14.322
And that assumes that
the nations of the world

1513
02:11:14.347 --> 02:11:16.715
work together to ration food.

1514
02:11:18.128 --> 02:11:19.564
Which they won't.

1515
02:11:21.158 --> 02:11:23.040
So I'd double the estimate.

1516
02:11:23.065 --> 02:11:24.904
And if you would truly
care about the children,

1517
02:11:24.929 --> 02:11:27.865
or anyone else for that
matter, you'd get on that ship.

1518
02:11:32.716 --> 02:11:34.885
I understand the stakes.

1519
02:11:36.334 --> 02:11:37.436
I do.

1520
02:11:41.459 --> 02:11:43.194
But I don't have it in me.

1521
02:11:49.333 --> 02:11:51.543
My mind is made up.

1522
02:11:54.830 --> 02:11:58.774
I'm sorry, but, uh

1523
02:11:58.798 --> 02:12:01.234
you just can't
talk me into it.

1524
02:12:02.112 --> 02:12:03.628
I'm sorry.

1525
02:12:04.781 --> 02:12:07.952
I'm not trying to talk
you into anything.

1526
02:12:09.224 --> 02:12:11.714
I am...

1527
02:12:11.746 --> 02:12:15.349
trying to make you understand

1528
02:12:15.374 --> 02:12:17.041
what I'm about to do next.

